      "node_id": 0,
      "node_type": "claude",
      "title": "Lovely, thank you",
      "uuid": "ab6b35a29ac84c05898fe54a8cf3c807",
      "x": 1587.6521369552447,
      "y": -1194.0662796526303,
      "width": 868.3414465524736,
      "height": 122.0,
      "z_value": 10.0,
      "ports_visible": false,
      "emoji": "\ud83d\ude25",
      "depth_front": true,
      "folder_path": "C:\\Users\\thisg\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-thisg-Desktop-Intricate",
      "body_text": "\n\u203a we forgot to make an icon for the video node\n\nLet me find the VideoNode first to understand what it does, then craft an icon for it.\nThe icon files already exist (`icons/video_node.png` and `icons/video_node.ico`), but the icon isn't registered in `settings.toml`. Let me check the current icon section and take a look at the existing icon to see if it's a real icon or just a placeholder.\nThe icon exists and looks great \u2014 warm cream play button with film sprocket dots, matching the family style perfectly. It just needs to be registered in `settings.toml`. Let me find the icons section.\nFound it \u2014 the settings file is at `C:\\Users\\thisg\\Desktop\\The Settlers\\settings.toml`. The icon files exist and look good, just need to register the video icon. Let me add it.\nDone. The icon was already created (play button with film sprocket dots, warm cream on transparent \u2014 fits the family nicely), it just wasn't wired up. Added `video = \"video_node.ico\"` to `[theme.icons]` in `settings.toml`, so `Theme.iconVideo` will now res\nDone. The icon was already created (play button with film sprocket dots, warm cream on transparent \u2014 fits the family nicely), it just wasn't wired up. Added `video = \"video_node.ico\"` to `[theme.icons]` in `settings.toml`, so `Theme.iconVideo` will now resolve automatically.\nolve automatically.\n\n\n\u203a lovely, thanks, speaking icons, the zoom slider handle in the bottom toolbar, can you apply the curtains icon to it please?  it should have all the setup already to accept png icons as handles from PrettySlider\n\nDone. Added `use_scroll_icon=True` to the zoom slider at line 876. It'll now pick up the PNG handle icon from `[theme.sliders] slider_handle_icon` in settings.toml \u2014 make sure that key points to the curtains icon file (e.g. `slider_handle_icon = \"curtains_\nnode.ico\"`).\n\n\n\u203a lovely, thank you, and then we need to take the slider that is in the left sidebar under the buttons to create new nodes, and have that one do the same, use PrettySlider and pick up the same icon\n\nDone. The fog slider now uses `pretty_slider()` with `use_scroll_icon=True`, matching the zoom slider's pattern. It picks up the same scroll-handle icon from `settings.toml` and gets the themed groove/handle styling from `PrettySlider` instead of inline QS\nS.\n\n\n\u203a 2026-04-04 19:18:18 - nodal - TRACE - [boot:13] constructing IntricateApp window\n2026-04-04 19:18:18 - nodal - TRACE - [boot:13a] Theme.icon at window construction = <bound method Theme.icon of <class 'graphics.Theme.Theme'>>\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"C:\\Users\\thisg\\Desktop\\Intricate\\main_window.py\", line 636, in _on_fog_slider_changed\n    self.fog_progress.setValue(value)\n    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nAttributeError: 'IntricateApp' object has no attribute 'fog_progress'\n2026-04-04 19:18:19 - nodal - TRACE - [boot:14] IntricateApp window constructed\n2026-04-04 19:18:19 - nodal - TRACE - [boot:15] window shown \u2014 entering event loop\n\nThe `pretty_slider` helper sets the initial value during construction, which fires `valueChanged` before `fog_progress` is assigned on line 611. The guard skips the update during that early si\ngnal and works normally once both widgets exist.\n\n\n\u203a lovely, Thank you\n\n\n\nYou're welcome! Let me know whenever you need anything.\n",
      "input_text": "",
      "body_visible": false
    },
